# `mismatch`: a function taking an `Error` is no function taking a `~Nat`: a `~Nat` that
# succeeded is no `Error` (Semantics ch. 10: an `Error` is a `~T`'s failure, not the other
# way round). Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
Msg: fn Error -> Text
fn Msg e = e.message

Use: fn (fn ~Nat -> Text), ~Nat -> Text
fn Use F, ~x = F ~x

Shown: fn Nat -> Text
fn Shown n = Use Msg, (~ n)
